The output-layer dimension table — **33 emotion words and their three-tier
split** (basic 11 / compound 18 / contemporary 4) — is derived from
**dsh-mood** by 一叶子秋 (`JMX-4869`), copied on 2026-10-29 from version
`0.14.16`.

dsh-mood is distributed under the MIT License. Its copyright notice and
permission notice are reproduced below, as the MIT License requires.

- Source: https://github.com/JMX-4869/dsh-mood
- What we took: the list of 33 emotion words and their grouping
- What we did **not** take: the per-word `(valence, arousal)` coordinates, the
  input-to-middle-layer derivation, the `CFG` parameters, the check scripts and
  all conclusions — those are ours
- What we changed: three of its words (`撒娇` / `摆烂` / `破防`) describe
  actions or event outcomes rather than states, so we mark them as not
  participating in emotion-space lighting (see `NON_EMOTION_DIMS` in
  `appraisal.mjs`)

